  "result": "Perfect! All voucher tests pass. Here's a summary of the implementation:\n\n## Changes made:\n\n**1. Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"An invoice can only have one voucher.\"\n\n**2. Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n- **Modified `invoiceTotals` function**:\n  - Now accepts `invoice.voucher` property (optional)\n  - Added `voucher` field to return object (amount or 0 if not applied)\n  - Updated total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - Total still clamps at 0 with `Math.max(0, ...)`\n\n- **Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function**:\n  - Validates invoice status is 'draft' (error: NOT_DRAFT)\n  - Validates invoice doesn't already have a voucher (error: VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (error: AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n  - Does not mutate the original invoice\n\n**3. Added 14 comprehensive tests to `test/invoices.test.js`**:\n- **Basic functionality**: Apply voucher to draft invoice\n- **Status validation**: Error on issued/paid invoices\n- **Duplicate prevention**: Error when trying to apply second voucher\n- **Amount validation**: Errors for non-integer, zero, negative amounts\n- **Immutability**: Ensures original invoice is not mutated\n- **invoiceTotals integration**: \n  - Voucher field included in result\n  - Total calculation with voucher applied\n  - Proper subtraction formula\n  - Clamping negative total at 0\n  - Large voucher amounts\n- **Property preservation**: Other invoice properties maintained\n\n**Test results**: All 185 tests pass (171 existing + 14 new)",
